---
import { url } from "../lib/docs";
import "../styles/product-video.css";
---

<figure class="demo-player">
  <div class="product-video" data-product-video>
    <div class="product-video-screen">
      <video
        controls
        playsinline
        preload="none"
        poster={url("demos/duckpad-overview.jpg")}
        width="1920"
        height="1080"
        aria-label="Duckpad in one minute: build visual pipelines, explore results and version your work"
        aria-describedby="product-video-caption"
      >
        <source src={url("demos/duckpad-overview.mp4")} type="video/mp4" />
        <track
          kind="captions"
          src={url("demos/duckpad-overview.vtt")}
          srclang="en"
          label="English"
          default
        />
        Your browser cannot play this video.{" "}
        <a href={url("demos/duckpad-overview.mp4")}>
          Download the one-minute video.
        </a>
      </video>
      <button class="video-cover" type="button" data-cover hidden>
        <span class="video-cover-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path d="m9 5 11 7-11 7Z" />
          </svg>
        </span>
        <span>
          <strong data-cover-label>Watch the film</strong>
          <small>Duckpad in 60 seconds</small>
        </span>
      </button>
    </div>
    <div class="video-controls" role="group" aria-label="Video controls" hidden>
      <input
        class="video-seek"
        data-seek
        type="range"
        min="0"
        max="60"
        step="0.1"
        value="0"
        aria-label="Video progress"
        aria-valuetext="0:00 of 1:00"
        disabled
      />
      <div class="video-controls-row">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="video-button"
          data-play
          aria-label="Play video"
          title="Play video"
        >
          <svg class="icon-play" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="m8 5 11 7-11 7Z" />
          </svg>
          <svg class="icon-pause" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M8 5v14M16 5v14" />
          </svg>
        </button>
        <span class="video-time">
          <span data-time>0:00</span>
          <span class="video-time-divider">/</span>
          <span data-duration>1:00</span>
        </span>
        <span class="video-controls-title" aria-hidden="true">
          THE DUCKPAD FILM
        </span>
        <div class="video-volume">
          <button
            type="button"
            class="video-button"
            data-mute
            aria-label="Mute video"
            title="Mute video"
          >
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="m11 5-6 4H2v6h3l6 4Z" />
              <path
                class="icon-sound"
                d="M15 8a6 6 0 0 1 0 8m3-11a10 10 0 0 1 0 14"
              />
              <path class="icon-muted" d="m16 9 6 6m0-6-6 6" />
            </svg>
          </button>
          <input
            data-volume
            type="range"
            min="0"
            max="1"
            step="0.05"
            value="1"
            aria-label="Volume"
            aria-valuetext="100%"
          />
        </div>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="video-button video-captions"
          data-captions
          aria-label="English captions"
          aria-pressed="true"
          title="English captions"
        >
          CC
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="video-button"
          data-fullscreen
          aria-label="Enter fullscreen"
          title="Enter fullscreen"
          hidden
        >
          <svg class="icon-expand" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M8 3H3v5m13-5h5v5M3 16v5h5m13-5v5h-5" />
          </svg>
          <svg class="icon-collapse" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M3 8h5V3m8 0v5h5M8 21v-5H3m13 5v-5h5" />
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="video-message" role="status" hidden>
      <span data-message></span>{" "}
      <a href={url("demos/duckpad-overview.mp4")}>Open the video directly ↗</a>
    </p>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="product-video-caption">
    <span class="live-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Duckpad in one minute ·
    English narration · Real app footage, edited for pace{" "}
    <a href={url("docs/quickstart/")}>Build your first pipeline ↗</a>
  </figcaption>
  <details class="video-transcript">
    <summary>Read the video transcript</summary>
    <div>
      <p>
        Your next pipeline starts with a drag. Meet Duckpad. An open-source
        workspace for people who work with data.
      </p>
      <p>
        Drop a step onto the canvas. Connect your sources. Shape the flow. Use
        simple controls to filter, join, and transform. Or open the SQL when you
        want to go deeper.
      </p>
      <p>
        <em>On screen:</em> A Filter node is dragged into the Northstar
        pipeline, connected to Orders, and configured to keep amounts greater
        than 100. The Code workspace shows the SQL behind a transformation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Run with DuckDB, then explore the result right where you built it.
        Wonder where a number came from? Click it. Follow the calculation, all
        the way back to the source. Turn useful steps into reusable components.
      </p>
      <p>
        <em>On screen:</em> The Regional revenue report shows a value of 7,131.
        Clicking it opens a lineage graph with its 27 contributing source
        values. A nested component reveals the filter and aggregation it
        contains.
      </p>
      <p>
        And keep your work versioned with Git. Review what changed. Explore a
        branch. Build with the confidence to go back. From the first connection
        to a result you can explain. Duckpad. See the flow. Trust the result.
      </p>
      <p>
        <em>On screen:</em> Git history and version comparison lead into
        creating an independent working branch. The film closes with “Build your
        first pipeline.”
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>
</figure>

<script>
  import { enhanceProductVideo } from "../lib/product-video";
  document
    .querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-product-video]")
    .forEach(enhanceProductVideo);
</script>

<style>
  .video-transcript {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 15px 18px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .video-transcript > div {
    max-width: 75ch;
    margin: 18px auto 0;
  }
  .video-transcript p + p {
    margin-top: 14px;
  }
</style>
